      <div type="clause" n="57">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 57</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="57" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="114" ed="#liebermann"/>CI. Gif ceorl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.30"/> ceap forstilð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.31"/> ⁊ bireð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.32"/> into his ærne, ⁊ befehð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.33"/> þærinne mon, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> bið<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.17"/> se his dǽl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.34"/> synnig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.35"/> butan þa<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.36"/></hi> wife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.37"/> anu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, forðon hio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.38"/> sceal hire ealdore<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.39"/> hieran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.40"/>: gif hio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.38"/> dear mid aðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.41"/> gecyðan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hio<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.38"/> þæs forstolenan ne onbite<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.42"/>, nime hire<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.43"/> ðriddan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.44"/> sceat.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="45" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.45"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="57" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="114" ed="#liebermann"/>CI. Gif ciorl ceap forsteleþ ⁊ byrð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.1"/> into his huse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.13"/> (<hi rend="italic">ve</hi>l ærne), ⁊ hit mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.9"/> ðærinnne befehð, þonne bið<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.14"/> his dæl scyldig buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.9"/> þam wife anu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, forðon heo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.15"/> sceal hire hlaforde hyran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.1"/>: gif heo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.15"/> dear mid aþe gecyþan, ðæt heo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.15"/> þæs forstolenan ne onbite, nime hire ðriddan gescead.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.16"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="57" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="114" ed="#liebermann"/>Be cyrlisces mannes stale. Gyf ceorl ceap forstylð ⁊ bereð into his ærne, ⁊ [mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.4"/>] befehþ [hitt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.4"/>] ðærinne, ðonne [biþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.4"/>] his dæl synnig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.7"/> butan ðam wife anu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, forðan heo sceol hire ealdre hyran: gyf heo dear mid aðe gecyðan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> [h]eo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.8"/> ðæs forstolenan ne onbite, nime hire ðæne ðriddan dæl ðære æhta.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="57" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="115" ed="#liebermann"/>Si ceorl<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.19"/> aliquod captale furetur et deferat in suum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.20"/> ærne ([deorne] id est secretum habitaculum suum), et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.21"/> intercipiatur ibi, sit sue parti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.22"/> reus preter feminam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.23"/> eius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.24"/> solam, quia ipsa debet domino suo parere: si audeat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.25"/> iureiurando satisfacere, quod de ipso furto non gustauit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.26"/>, habeat (ipsa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Ine_57.lnote.oe.27"/>) suam terciam partem pecunie.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="54–56" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be cyrlisces mannes stale.] Gif ceorl ceap forstilð ⁊ bireð into his ærne<ptr type="editorNote" n="24" target="#Ine_57.attnote.fn.24"/>, ⁊<ptr type="editorNote" n="25" target="#Ine_57.attnote.fn.25"/> befehð þærinne mon, þonne bið se his dǽl synnig<ptr type="editorNote" n="26" target="#Ine_57.attnote.fn.26"/> butan þam wife anum, forðon hio sceal hire ealdore<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_57.attnote.fn.1"/> hieran: gif hio dear mid aðe gecyðan þæt hio þæs forstolenan ne onbite, nime hire ðriddan sceat<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_57.attnote.fn.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="61" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="420" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{CI} Gif ceorl ceap forstilð ⁊ bireð into his ærne, ⁊ befehð þærinne mon, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> bið se his dǽl synnig butan þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> wife anu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, forðon hio sceal hire ealdore hieran. Gif hio dear mid aðe gecyðan, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hio þæs forstolenan ne onbite, nime hire ðriddan sceat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="115" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn ein Ehemann Fahrhabe stiehlt und in sein Haus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.1"/> bringt, und man ertappt (es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.2"/>) darin, dann ist jener für seinen Theil [zwar] schuldig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.3"/>, nur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.4"/> ohne die Ehefrau, weil sie ihrem Eheherrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.5"/> gehorchen soll: wenn sie durch Eid zu beweisen wagt, dass sie von dem Gestohlenen nicht genoss<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.6"/>, nehme sie ihren<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.7"/> dritten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.8"/> Heller<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.9"/> (des Haushaltsvermögens<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_57.lnote.de.10"/>).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a husband steals movable goods and brings them into his house, and (they) are seized there, then he is [indeed] guilty for his share, but not his wife, because she must obey her lord: if she dares to prove by oath that she did not partake of the stolen goods, let her take her third penny (of the household property).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="55" ed="#attenborough"/>If a husband steals a beast and carries it into his house, and it is seized therein, he shall forfeit his share [of the household property<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_57.attnote.n.1"/>]—his wife only being exempt, since she must obey her lord. If she dare declare, with an oath, that she has not tasted the stolen [meat], she shall retain her third of the [household] property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="406" ed="#whitelock"/>If a husband steals any cattle and brings it into his house, and it is seized therein, he is guilty for his part, but without his wife, for she must obey her lord; if she dare declare with an oath that she did not taste of the stolen meat, she is to receive her third portion.<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Ine_57.whinote.n.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="421" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> steals property and takes it into his house, and it is caught therein, then he is liable for his portion [of the household goods]; only his wife is exempted, because she must obey her superior. If she dare declare on oath, that she did not partake of the stolen goods, let her take her third portion [of the household goods].</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_76">II Cn 76</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_76-1">II Cn 76.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_76-1b">II Cn 76.1b</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="421"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_7">Ine 7</ref> <quote>For a somewhat different interpretation of the wife's liability, compare §7.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><ref target="clause:IICn_76">II Cn 76–76.1b</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="473"><ref target="clause:IICn_76">II Cn 76</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="367"><ref target="clause:IICn_76">II Cn 76–76.1</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. eingefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inserted in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">darüber im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi> scyldig</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">above it in the 16th cent. scyldig</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">h (<hi rend="italic">vor</hi> eo) <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">h (before eo) in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> ceorlus f. a. ca. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; ceorlus f. a. ca. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> su. æ. [deorne <hi rend="italic">K</hi>] i. e. sec. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> ha. su. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only su. æ. [deorne K] i. e. sec. Lond; only ha. su. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et i. i. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et i. i. lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">partis <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">partis Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">animam <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">animam R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eius — parere <hi rend="italic">Lond, statt dessen nur</hi> suam <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eius — parere Lond, instead of which only suam the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_57.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eum <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eum added by Lond</seg></note>
